          "source_cycle": 2,
          "source_completion_round": 2,
          "body": "Align the shipped default process preset with the new named stoichiometric constant. `ProcessParams::default()` now uses `NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N` in `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs:337-338`, but the runtime default preset loaded from `crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml:52-54` still hard-codes `0.1428`, and scenario startup converts that preset into live params in `crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs:346-349`. As written, two code paths that both claim to use the default process parameters will consume different alkalinity and can diverge in deterministic comparisons.",
